      "tool_uses": [],
      "assistant_text": "The **Guarded Write Journal** page (from [[write-journal]]) describes a mechanism for providing transaction-like safety when writing files in Grimoire\u0027s guarded tool execution model.\n\nHere\u0027s what it covers:\n\n1. **Core purpose**: Before the guarded tool executor overwrites any file, it records the file\u0027s prior state\u2014either its previous content if it existed, or a marker that it didn\u0027t exist\u2014into an in-memory write journal.\n\n2. **Rollback mechanism**: If an agent run fails (due to a turn cap being exceeded, an unrecoverable error, or denied writes), the journal can roll back every recorded write in reverse order\u2014restoring previous content for files that existed and deleting newly created files.\n\n3. **Transaction semantics**: This journal approach gives each run \u0022all-or-nothing\u0022 semantics for its writes without needing a database transaction\u2014the journal itself serves as the transaction log, held entirely in process memory for the duration of a single run.\n\n4. **Query agent note**: The Query agent doesn\u0027t use the rollback path since it has no write tool at all; the journal type exists in the shared agent runtime library but is only populated by agents that actually write.",
      "input_tokens": 5538,
      "output_tokens": 264
    }
